    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0998" n="904" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg904"/>

                <head>No. 535.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bell
                        to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The
                                Hague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-09-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 20, 1887</date>. (Received
                        October 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 266.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith, for
                    the information of the Department, two copies,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d535-f1"/>
                    in the Dutch text, of the speech pronounced by His Majesty the King on the
                    opening of the session of the States-General on the 19th instant.</p>
                <p>It will be seen that His Majesty, after thanking the people for the loyalty and
                    devotion shown on the occasion of the celebration of the seventieth anniversary
                    of his birth, expressed the hope that the constitutional revision bill would be
                    sanctioned by the chambers.</p>
                <p>He declared his relations to be most satisfactory with all foreign powers, and
                    expressed satisfaction at the condition of the army and navy, as well as the
                    finances of the country.</p>
                <p>He announced that measures would be submitted for the consideration of the
                    chambers tending to advance the agricultural and commercial interests of the
                    country.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Isaac Bell, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
